-- =====================================================================
-- Session 154 — Matt 17 extras-tier cross-references (single chapter)
-- =====================================================================
-- Adds Matt 17's extras-tier rows + threads to the cross-reference
-- corpus. Continues the S131 (Matt 1-2) -> S146 (Matt 16) extras-tier
-- coverage; Matt 17 lands as the transfiguration + Eliyahu-is-come-
-- already + demoniac-boy-and-mustard-seed-faith + second-passion-
-- prediction + temple-tax-and-fish-coin chapter. Five framework-bearing
-- narrative movements anchor the chapter:
--
--   (a) the transfiguration proper on the high mountain (vv.1-8) — the
--       King''s-face-shining-as-the-sun and raiment-white-as-the-light;
--       Mosheh (Moses) and Eliyahu (Elijah) appearing in glorified-form
--       talking-with-him of the *exodus* the King would accomplish at
--       Yerushalayim (Jerusalem); the bright-cloud overshadowing as the
--       Tanakh-kavod (glory)-cloud pattern; the Father''s-voice combining
--       Tehillim (Psalm) 2:7 Davidic-Royal-Son enthronement-substance,
--       Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 42:1 Suffering-Servant election, and Devarim
--       (Deuteronomy) 18:15 prophet-like-unto-Mosheh authoritative-
--       hearing-substance in one utterance; the disciples'' fall-on-the-
--       face the Tanakh-theophany-response (Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 6:5,
--       Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 1:28, Daniel 10:9, Hitgalut (Revelation)
--       1:17); the King''s-touch-and-*arise-and-be-not-afraid* the
--       Tanakh-heavenly-messenger-pattern the King occupies because he
--       IS the One the messengers served; *Yahusha (Jesus) only* as the
--       final-correction to Kefa''s (Peter''s)-three-tabernacles-proposal
--       — the King is the tabernacle of John 1:14, one tabernacle
--       suffices.
--   (b) the coming-down-from-the-mountain charge to silence-until-the-
--       resurrection and the King''s explicit-identification of Yochanan
--       (John) the Immerser as the Eliyahu (Elijah) who was to come
--       (vv.9-13) — both-fulfillments: future-tense *Eliyahu (Elijah)
--       truly shall first come, and restore all things* (Hitgalut
--       (Revelation) 11''s two-witnesses + Acts 3:21''s *times of
--       restitution of all things*); past-tense *Eliyahu (Elijah) is
--       come already, and they knew him not, but have done unto him
--       whatsoever they listed* — Yochanan (John) the Immerser as the
--       Eliyahu (Elijah)-pattern-prophet at the first-coming per
--       Malachi 4:5-6 and Matthew 11:14, with Herod-Antipas and
--       Herodias as the Achav (Ahab) and Izevel (Jezebel) of the
--       first-century-recapitulation; *likewise shall also the Son of
--       Adam suffer of them* ties the King''s-coming-passion to the
--       Eliyahu (Elijah)-pattern-prophet''s-martyrdom.
--   (c) the demoniac-boy at the foot of the mountain and the mustard-
--       seed-faith teaching with the prayer-and-fasting saying
--       (vv.14-21) — the disciples'' *unbelief* (*oligopistia* — little-
--       faith, same word at Matt 14:31 and 16:8); the King''s-rebuke of
--       *faithless and perverse generation* echoing Mosheh''s (Moses'')
--       song against the wilderness-generation at Devarim (Deuteronomy)
--       32:5, 20; the mustard-seed-faith substance of Matt 13:31-32 as
--       qualitative-not-quantitative; *howbeit this kind goeth not out
--       but by prayer and fasting* (v.21) — fasting remains a kingdom-
--       substance-discipline.
--   (d) the second passion-prediction (vv.22-23) — *the Son of Adam
--       shall be betrayed (paradidotai — delivered-up, the Yeshayahu
--       (Isaiah) 53 Suffering-Servant verb) into the hands of men: and
--       they shall kill him, and the third day he shall be raised
--       again*; the threefold-prediction pattern (Matt 16:21, 17:22-23,
--       20:17-19) producing the disciples'' progression of learning the
--       *must* (*dei*) of the passion.
--   (e) the temple-tax pericope / Kefa-fishing-the-coin (vv.24-27) —
--       the half-shekel temple-tax as Shemot (Exodus) 30:11-15''s
--       atonement-money (*to make an atonement for your souls*); the
--       King''s-question *of whom do the kings of the earth take custom
--       or tribute? of their own children, or of strangers?* applying
--       the Tanakh-monarchic-precedent; *then are the children free*
--       naming the categorical-architecture — the King is the Son of
--       the One whose Temple this is; *notwithstanding, lest we should
--       offend them* — *skandalisōmen* — the kingdom-citizen does not
--       throw the kingdom-exemption in the face of the still-unawakened-
--       system in a way that creates a stumbling-block; the miraculous
--       coin-in-the-fish''s-mouth (*statēr* = four-drachmas = exactly
--       two half-shekels for the King and Kefa (Peter), no remainder)
--       as the Owner-of-the-sea''s-sovereign-direction (Tehillim
--       (Psalm) 8:6-8''s Adamic-dominion + Yonah (Jonah) 1:17''s great-
--       fish-appointed); the half-shekel-as-atonement-money pre-figures
--       the cross — the categorically-exempt King pays the atonement-
--       substance the categorically-bound owe.
--
-- Matt 17 reading-target: the chapter walks five movements with the
-- Tanakh-substance carrying the heaviest framework-bearing anchors
-- directly (Shemot (Exodus) 24:16-18 for the six-days-and-the-seventh-
-- Sinai-pattern; Shemot (Exodus) 34:29 + 2 Corinthians 3:13 for the
-- Mosheh''s-face-shining-by-reflection-and-fading contrast against the
-- King''s-face-shining-by-emanation; Daniel 7:9 Ancient-of-Days and
-- Daniel 10:5-6 Man-Clothed-in-Linen and Hitgalut (Revelation)
-- 1:13-16''s *one like unto the Son of Adam* for the consistent
-- glorified-Son-of-Adam Tanakh-and-apostolic-architecture; Devarim
-- (Deuteronomy) 18:15-19 + Acts 3:22-23 for the prophet-like-unto-
-- Mosheh; Malachi 4:5-6 + Acts 3:21 for the restoration-of-all-things;
-- Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 53 + Zekharyah (Zechariah) 13:7 for the suffering-
-- servant the second-passion-prediction draws-from; Shemot (Exodus)
-- 30:11-15 + 2 Kings 12:4-16 + Nehemiah 10:32-33 for the half-shekel-
-- atonement-money temple-tax architecture; Tehillim (Psalm) 8:6-8 +
-- Yonah (Jonah) 1:17 for the Adamic-dominion-over-the-fish; Hebrews
-- 7:27 for the once-for-all atonement the half-shekel-pre-figures).
-- The extras-library adds five framework-bearing thread-clusters:
--   Thread 1 (FRAMEWORK-MAJOR): Ascension of Isaiah 9-10''s seventh-
--     heaven Great-Glory + Lord/Beloved-in-submission + Beloved-
--     descending-and-becoming-like-the-likeness-of-each-heaven
--     architecture — the deepest external-witness to the Formless-
--     Father/Formed-Son nature-of-God-teaching the transfiguration''s
--     veil-pulled-back exposes (Yoshi-flagged in seed.py:EDITION_
--     PROFILES["ascension-isaiah"] as the *external witness ... that
--     aligns with what the spirit revealed to me about the formless
--     father and the formed of the formless*).
--   Thread 2 (FRAMEWORK-MAJOR): 1 Enoch 14''s throne-vision + 46-62''s
--     Son-of-Adam-Parables architecture — the wisdom-stream''s
--     articulation of the glorified-Son-of-Adam in-heavenly-form the
--     transfiguration shows in pre-resurrection-foretaste.
--   Thread 3: Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48''s Eliyahu (Elijah)-as-
--     reproof-prophet substance — the wisdom-stream''s direct
--     articulation of the Malachi 4:5-6 turn-the-heart substance the
--     King applies at vv.10-13 to Yochanan (John) the Immerser as
--     the Eliyahu (Elijah)-pattern-prophet at the first-coming.
--   Thread 4: Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 16 + Wisdom of Solomon 5 + 2
--     Esdras (4 Ezra) 7 on the faithless-and-perverse-generation
--     substance — the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Devarim
--     (Deuteronomy) 32 long-arc the King''s-rebuke at v.17 invokes.
--   Thread 5: Wisdom of Solomon 2:13-20''s prefiguring-passage on the
--     righteous-one-as-the-son-of-Yahuah persecuted-and-vindicated
--     substance — connecting both the second-passion-prediction at
--     vv.22-23 AND the temple-tax-Son-pays-for-the-categorically-bound
--     pre-figuring at vv.24-27 to the wisdom-stream''s direct
--     prefiguring.
--
-- Jubilees, Jasher, Adam-Eve Conflict, Apocalypse of Abraham, and
-- Sonnini''s Acts of Paul do not surface framework-bearing Matt 17
-- connections at S154 (Apocalypse of Abraham 17-18''s ascension-vision
-- is thematically-adjacent to the transfiguration-cloud substance but
-- the Ascension of Isaiah 9-10 carries the framework-major load more
-- directly per the Yoshi-S32 sourcing-decision that elevated AI to its
-- own edition for exactly this nature-of-God witnessing-substance;
-- Sonnini''s Acts of Paul is the post-resurrection lost-sheep-mission
-- extension and does not bear on Matt 17''s pre-resurrection narrative).
-- Historical-witness editions (Josephus, M.R. James''s apocryphal NT,
-- Lightfoot''s Apostolic Fathers) remain deferred from V1 cross-refs
-- per the historical-witness one-way rule. The lookup view retains the
-- S146 edition set for forward compatibility.
--
-- Five PROPOSED threads at extras-tier:
--   1. `the-formless-father-and-the-formed-son-witnessed-in-ascension-of-isaiah`            (sort 307)
--   2. `the-son-of-adam-glorified-in-1-enoch-throne-vision-and-parables`                    (sort 308)
--   3. `eliyahu-as-reproof-prophet-turning-the-heart-in-sirach-48`                          (sort 309)
--   4. `the-faithless-and-perverse-generation-in-sirach-wisdom-of-solomon-and-2-esdras`     (sort 310)
--   5. `the-just-man-as-son-of-yahuah-condemned-and-vindicated-in-wisdom-of-solomon-2`      (sort 311)
--
-- 21 new cross_references rows at tier_required=''extras'' (Library
-- tier, $4.99) + 5 new cross_reference_threads at tier_required=
-- ''complete_study'' (Companion tier, $9.99). The tier split honors the
-- chapter-end-card architecture established at S146 and prior: Layer 1
-- (per-verse cross-refs) visible to Library readers; Layer 2 (framework
-- thread callouts with summary_md + member_notes) gated at Companion.
-- Every member-note passes the 12 Red Lines and the 12-point editorial
-- checklist. The seed-mechanism per framework-deep''s *Paternal Seed
-- and the Marriage-Covenant Absorption* section + Red Line #7
-- augmentation does not surface in Matt 17 (no foreign-origin
-- individuals or seed-distinction substance in the chapter — the
-- chapter is internal to the disciples and the demoniac-boy''s-father
-- and the temple-tax-collectors, all within-the-covenant-people).
-- Hebrew names with internal apostrophes (Yashar''el, Ya''aqov,
-- Yechezk''el, Yo''el, Sha''ul, Mikha''el, Mosheh''s, King''s, Father''s,
-- Yahuah''s, Yochanan''s, Kefa''s, etc.) and English possessives
-- (wisdom-stream''s, master''s, Father''s, King''s, system''s, etc.) are
-- escaped per SQL single-quoted-string-literal convention (every
-- internal ' doubled to '').
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on every INSERT.
-- =====================================================================

\echo 'Session 154 — Matt 17 extras-tier cross-references migration starting...'
BEGIN;

-- Verse-lookup temp view. Mirrors the S146 view; retained for forward
-- compatibility even though Matt 17 surfaces only canon + enoch +
-- apocrypha + ascension-isaiah at S154.
CREATE TEMP VIEW _s154_xref_lookup AS
SELECT
    e.slug AS edition_slug,
    b.slug AS book_slug,
    c.chapter_number,
    v.verse_number,
    v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v
  JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id = c.id
  JOIN books    b ON c.book_id    = b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id = e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN (
       'canon',
       'enoch',
       'jubilees',
       'jasher',
       'apocrypha',
       'apocrypha-charles-vol1',
       'pseudepigrapha',
       'adam-eve-conflict',
       'apocalypse-of-abraham',
       'ascension-isaiah',
       'sonnini-acts-29'
   );

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insert 21 extras-tier cross_references rows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH input(src_edition, src_slug, src_ch, src_v,
           tgt_edition, tgt_slug, tgt_ch, tgt_v, note) AS (VALUES

  -- Thread 1: the-formless-father-and-the-formed-son-witnessed-in-ascension-of-isaiah
  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 2, 'ascension-isaiah', 'ascension-isaiah', 9, 27,
   '*And I saw a certain One standing, whose glory surpassed that of all, and His glory was great and wonderful.* Ascension of Isaiah 9:27 names the external-witness articulation of the Formed-Son standing-before-the-Father in the seventh-heaven. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:2''s *his face did shine as the sun, and his raiment was white as the light.* The transfiguration pulls back the form-of-servant-veil (Philippians 2:6-7) so the disciples see the Formed-essence the King had laid aside in the incarnation. Ascension of Isaiah''s seventh-heaven vision shows the same Formed-One in the pre-incarnational standing-position before the Great Glory — the One whose-glory-surpassed-that-of-all-the-angels-and-archangels-of-the-six-lower-heavens. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture at the heavenly-substance-register; the transfiguration shows the same substance at the earthly-witnessed-register. Per Yoshi''s S32 sourcing-note (api/seed.py:EDITION_PROFILES["ascension-isaiah"]), AI is the *first witness* aligning with the framework''s Formless-Father / Formed-of-the-Formless nature-of-God teaching — pre-Nicene, late-1st / early-2nd CE, before the Constantine-era Trinity-construct hardened. FRAMEWORK-MAJOR.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 3, 'ascension-isaiah', 'ascension-isaiah', 9, 33,
   '*And whilst he was still speaking, I saw another Glorious One who was like Him, and the righteous drew nigh and worshipped and praised, and I also praised with them.* Ascension of Isaiah 9:33 names the seventh-heaven witnessing the Lord and the *another Glorious One who was like Him* — the Beloved standing beside the One-whose-glory-surpasses. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:3''s *there appeared unto them Mosheh (Moses) and Eliyahu (Elijah) talking with him.* Matt 17 shows the King in conversation with the two Tanakh-witnesses Mosheh (Moses) and Eliyahu (Elijah); Ascension of Isaiah 9:33 shows the upper-heaven counterpart — the Beloved standing in glorified-conversation with the One-whose-glory-surpasses. The pattern Matt 17 enacts in the high-mountain-theophany at the historical-pivot is the architecture Ascension of Isaiah had named at the heavenly-substance-register. The wisdom-stream-substance and the gospel-substance cohere.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 5, 'ascension-isaiah', 'ascension-isaiah', 9, 37,
   '*And I saw the great glory, the eyes of my spirit being open, and I could not thereupon see, nor yet could the angel who was with me, nor all the angels whom I had seen worship Yahuah (the Lord).* Ascension of Isaiah 9:37 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the Great-Glory the formless-substance the eye-cannot-bear-to-look-upon names. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:5''s *behold, a bright cloud overshadowed them: and behold a voice out of the cloud, which said, This is my beloved Son.* The bright-cloud at the transfiguration is the Tanakh-kavod (glory)-cloud that marks the Father''s-presence (Shemot (Exodus) 16:10, 40:34-35, 1 Kings 8:10-11); Ascension of Isaiah 9:37 names the same Father''s-substance at the heavenly-register — the Great-Glory the eye-of-the-prophet-cannot-bear-to-look-upon. The framework reads this in continuity with John 1:18''s *no man hath seen Elohim (God) at any time; the only begotten Son, which is in the bosom of the Father, he hath declared him* — the Father is the Formless-Source; the Son is the Formed-Voice through whom the Formless is declared.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 5, 'ascension-isaiah', 'ascension-isaiah', 10, 7,
   '*And I heard the voice of the Most High, the Father of my Lord, saying to my Yahuah (Lord) Messiah (Christ) who will be called Yahusha (Jesus).* Ascension of Isaiah 10:7 names THE direct external-witness verbal-anchor for the Father-speaking-to-the-Son substance the transfiguration enacts at Matt 17:5. The framework reads the verses together: the Father''s-voice from the bright-cloud on the high mountain (*this is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; hear ye him*) is the same Father''s-voice Ascension of Isaiah witnesses at the heavenly-register speaking-to-the-Beloved-by-name. AI 10:7 names the Beloved''s pre-incarnational name as *Yahusha (Jesus)* — the same name the King carries at the historical-incarnation; the wisdom-stream had named the substance centuries before the gospels articulated it at the earthly-pivot. The framework reads this as FRAMEWORK-MAJOR for the nature-of-God teaching: the Father is the Most-High; the Son is the Lord-of-the-Most-High''s-speaking; the speaking-Father and the spoken-to-Son are the architecture both AI and the gospels witness.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 8, 'ascension-isaiah', 'ascension-isaiah', 10, 9,
   '*And thou wilt become like unto the likeness of all who are in the five heavens.* Ascension of Isaiah 10:9 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Beloved''s-kenotic-descent substance — the Formed-Son becomes-like-the-likeness-of-each-heaven through which he descends, taking-the-form-of-the-creatures-of-each-level, culminating in becoming-like-the-form-of-man in the lowest descent. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:8''s *they saw no man, save Yahusha (Jesus) only.* The form-of-the-King the disciples see at the close of the transfiguration is the form-of-the-servant the kenosis-descent had-taken-on per Philippians 2:7. Ascension of Isaiah 10:9-10 articulates the kenosis-architecture at the wisdom-stream-register; the transfiguration shows the brief-pulling-back-of-the-servant-form-veil to reveal the underlying Formed-essence; *Yahusha (Jesus) only* names the return-to-the-servant-form for the continued-walking-of-the-incarnation through the cross-and-resurrection. The wisdom-stream and the gospel cohere at the kenosis-and-veil-pulling-back architecture.'),

  -- Thread 2: the-son-of-adam-glorified-in-1-enoch-throne-vision-and-parables
  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 2, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 14, 20,
   '*And the Great Glory sat thereon, and His raiment shone more brightly than the sun and was whiter than any snow.* 1 Enoch 14:20 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the *raiment whiter than snow* substance the transfiguration shows at the form-of-the-King-on-the-mountain. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:2''s *his raiment was white as the light.* The throne-vision of 1 Enoch 14 shows the Great-Glory in raiment-whiter-than-snow at the heavenly-register; the transfiguration shows the form-of-the-Formed-Son with raiment-white-as-the-light at the earthly-historical-register; the substance is the same. The framework reads this in continuity with Daniel 7:9''s Ancient-of-Days whose-garment-was-white-as-snow and Hitgalut (Revelation) 1:14''s *one like unto the Son of Adam ... his head and his hairs were white like wool, as white as snow.* The Tanakh-and-wisdom-stream-and-apostolic-stream all witness the same glorified-form-substance the King shows the disciples on the high mountain.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 6, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 14, 21,
   '*None of the angels could enter and could behold His face by reason of the magnificence and glory, and no flesh could behold Him.* 1 Enoch 14:21 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the no-flesh-could-behold-Him substance — the Tanakh-theophany-response of the prophet-falling-on-his-face the architecture extends to the angels-themselves. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:6''s *and when the disciples heard it, they fell on their face, and were sore afraid.* The disciples'' fall-on-the-face at the transfiguration is the universal-Tanakh-theophany-response (Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 6:5, Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 1:28, Daniel 10:9, Hitgalut (Revelation) 1:17); 1 Enoch 14:21 names the same architecture at the heavenly-register — even the angels-themselves cannot-behold-His-face. The substance the disciples experience on the mountain operates at the floor-of-the-architecture that applies-universally across the Tanakh-and-wisdom-stream-and-gospel pattern.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 5, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 46, 1,
   '*And there I saw One who had a head of days, and His head was white like wool, and with Him was another being whose countenance had the appearance of a man, and his face was full of graciousness, like one of the holy angels.* 1 Enoch 46:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Head-of-Days-with-the-One-whose-countenance-had-the-appearance-of-a-man substance — the Parables-of-Enoch had carried the Father-and-Son architecture centuries before the gospels articulated it at the gospel-pivot. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:5''s *behold, a bright cloud overshadowed them: and behold a voice out of the cloud, which said, This is my beloved Son.* The Father''s-voice from the bright-cloud declares the Son; 1 Enoch 46:1 names the same Father-and-Son architecture at the heavenly-throne-register. The wisdom-stream and the gospel cohere at the Head-of-Days / Formless-Father + the-One-whose-countenance-had-the-appearance-of-a-man / Formed-Son architecture per the framework''s nature-of-God reading.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 5, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 49, 2,
   '*For he is mighty in all the secrets of righteousness, and unrighteousness shall disappear as a shadow, and have no continuance; because the Elect One stands before Yahuah (the Lord) of Spirits.* 1 Enoch 49:2 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the Elect-One-standing-before-Yahuah-of-Spirits substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:5''s Father''s-voice declaring *this is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.* The Beloved-Son standing-on-the-mountain to whom the Father''s-voice is directed is the Elect-One 1 Enoch 49:2 had named the wisdom-stream-substance for. The framework reads this in continuity with Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 42:1''s *behold my servant, whom I uphold; mine elect, in whom my soul delighteth* the Father''s-voice combines into the declaration; the wisdom-stream-anchor and the Tanakh-anchor cohere at the Elect-One / mine-elect architecture the Father''s-voice articulates at the transfiguration-pivot.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 2, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 62, 5,
   '*And there shall stand up in that day all the kings and the mighty, and the exalted and those who hold the earth, and they shall see and recognise how he sits on the throne of his glory.* 1 Enoch 62:5 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the Son-of-Adam-sitting-on-the-throne-of-his-glory substance — the eschatological-vindication-vision that mirrors what the transfiguration shows in pre-resurrection-foretaste-form. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:2''s *and was transfigured before them: and his face did shine as the sun.* The transfiguration is the disciples'' pre-resurrection foretaste of the glorified-Son-of-Adam-on-the-throne-of-his-glory that 1 Enoch 62 names the eschatological-day-vision for. The disciples on the high mountain see in compressed-vision-form what the wisdom-stream had named as the day-when-the-Son-of-Adam-is-publicly-recognized-as-the-One-on-the-throne. The framework reads this in continuity with the *some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the Son of Adam coming in his kingdom* of Matt 16:28 — the transfiguration is the immediate-narrative-foretaste of the broader eschatological-second-coming-vindication.'),

  -- Thread 3: eliyahu-as-reproof-prophet-turning-the-heart-in-sirach-48
  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 10, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 48, 1,
   '*Then stood up Elias the prophet as fire, and his word burned like a lamp.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48:1 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the Eliyahu (Elijah)-as-prophet-of-fire substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:10''s *why then say the scribes that Eliyahu (Elijah) must first come?* The disciples'' question draws on the scribal-eschatology of Malachi 4:5-6''s *behold, I will send you Eliyahu (Elijah) the prophet before the coming of the great and dreadful day of Yahuah (the LORD)*; Sirach 48:1 names the wisdom-stream''s carrying-forward of the Eliyahu (Elijah)-pattern at the apocryphal-register, naming the prophet-of-fire whose-word-burned-like-a-lamp the disciples have just seen in glorified-form on the mountain (the Eliyahu (Elijah) of v.3) and whom the King is about to identify with Yochanan (John) the Immerser at the first-coming-fulfillment.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 11, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 48, 4,
   '*O Elias, how were you honoured in your wondrous deeds! and who may glory like to you!* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48:4 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Eliyahu (Elijah)-honoured-in-wondrous-deeds substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:11''s *Eliyahu (Elijah) truly shall first come, and restore all things.* The King''s-answer carries-forward both-fulfillments: the future-tense Eliyahu (Elijah) of the broader-restoration-of-all-things (Hitgalut (Revelation) 11''s two-witnesses + Acts 3:21''s *times of restitution of all things*) AND the past-tense Eliyahu (Elijah) of Yochanan (John) the Immerser at the first-coming. Sirach 48:4 names the wisdom-stream substance the Tanakh-Eliyahu (Elijah) carried at the prophetic-deeds-register; the King names the substance at the broader-eschatological-restoration-register; the wisdom-stream and the gospel cohere at the Eliyahu (Elijah)-as-restoration-pattern architecture.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 12, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 48, 10,
   '*Who were ordained for reproofs in their times, to pacify the wrath of the judgment of Yahuah (God), before it brake forth into fury, and to turn the heart of the father unto the son, and to set up the tribes of Yashar''el (Jacob).* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48:10 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the turn-the-heart-of-the-father-unto-the-son + set-up-the-tribes-of-Yashar''el substance — Sirach 48:10 carries Malachi 4:5-6 forward at the wisdom-stream-register, with the additional-articulation-of-the-tribes-of-Yashar''el (Jacob) substance the apostolic-Acts-3:21 *times of restitution of all things* will articulate at the apostolic-register. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:12''s *Eliyahu (Elijah) is come already, and they knew him not, but have done unto him whatsoever they listed. Likewise shall also the Son of Adam suffer of them.* The wisdom-stream had named the Eliyahu (Elijah)-prophet-of-reproofs at the prefiguring-register; the King names the operative-form at the first-coming-fulfillment in Yochanan (John) the Immerser, with the Eliyahu (Elijah)-pattern-prophet''s-martyrdom at the hands of Herod-Antipas and Herodias (the Achav (Ahab) and Izevel (Jezebel) of the first-century-recapitulation) tying-forward to the King''s-own-coming-passion. The framework reads the set-up-the-tribes-of-Yashar''el substance in continuity with Red Line #11''s ingathering-of-the-paternal-blood-remnant-of-all-twelve-tribes architecture — the Eliyahu (Elijah)-restoration the wisdom-stream names IS the gathering-of-the-scattered-seed the framework reads across the prophets.'),

  -- Thread 4: the-faithless-and-perverse-generation-in-sirach-wisdom-of-solomon-and-2-esdras
  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 17, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 16, 1,
   '*Desire not a multitude of unprofitable children, neither delight in ungodly sons.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 16:1 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the unprofitable-and-ungodly-generation substance — the diagnostic against the multitude-of-children-without-the-fear-of-Yahuah the surrounding-context Sirach 16:1-14 unfolds. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:17''s *O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you?* The King''s-rebuke is generation-wide, not narrowly disciple-aimed; the Greek *genea apistos kai diestrammenē* — *faithless and twisted generation* — echoes Mosheh''s (Moses'') song against the wilderness-generation at Devarim (Deuteronomy) 32:5, 20 (*a perverse and crooked generation* / *a very froward generation, children in whom is no faith*). Sirach 16:1-14 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the same architecture at the wisdom-instruction-register. The wilderness-generation''s-faithlessness was the substance the prophets named through the long-arc of Yashar''el (Israel)''s history; the faithlessness reaches the King''s-day in the religious-system of the leadership and the broader-people''s-disposition.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 17, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 5, 6,
   '*Therefore have we erred from the way of truth, and the light of righteousness hath not shined unto us, and the sun of righteousness rose not upon us.* Wisdom of Solomon 5:6 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the post-judgment-confession-of-the-ungodly substance — the day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-revealing-the-ungodly''s-blindness pattern. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:17''s *faithless and perverse generation.* The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the generation-that-erred-from-the-way-of-truth at the prophetic-register; the King names the operative-form at the gospel-pivot. The framework reads this in continuity with the cause-and-effect-of-hearing per Red Line #11 — the generation-that-cannot-hear is the one for which the light-of-righteousness has-not-shined; the sun-of-righteousness will rise upon those who do-hear (Malachi 4:2''s *unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings*); the rising-or-not-rising is downstream-of-the-prior-hearing-or-not-hearing.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 17, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 7, 48,
   '*O thou Adam, what hast thou done? for though it was thou that sinned, the fall was not thine alone, but ours also that come of thee.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:48 names the wisdom-stream articulation of the generation-after-generation-inheriting-the-Adam-fall substance — the corporate-inheritance of the Bereshit (Genesis) 3 wound across the generations. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:17''s *faithless and perverse generation* — the King''s-rebuke names a substance that has-been-running-in-the-generations-of-Adam since the fall. 2 Esdras 7:48 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the same generation-after-generation pattern. The framework reads this carefully — the inherited-Adam-wound is the cause of the perverse-and-twisted-substance the King names; the kingdom-cure is the new-heart of Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27, the breaking-of-the-generational-pattern through the Spirit-internalized-Torah, NOT the inherited-Christian-Augustinian original-sin doctrine that collapses the architecture into a forensic-substitutionary-juridical-transaction.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 20, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 16, 6,
   '*In the congregation of the ungodly shall a fire be kindled; and in a rebellious nation wrath is set on fire.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 16:6 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the consequences-on-the-rebellious-nation substance — the kindling-of-the-wrath the wilderness-generation incurred at Devarim (Deuteronomy) 32 carried-forward to the apocryphal-stream. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:20''s mustard-seed-faith teaching — the King''s-rebuke at v.17 names the generation-substance; the King''s-instruction at v.20 names the qualitative-faith-substance that operates against-the-generation-pattern. The mustard-seed-faith of the right-substance, even small-in-quantity, breaks-the-mountain-of-the-rebellious-system; the same Spirit who-moves-the-mountain is the Spirit who-internalizes-the-Torah and breaks-the-generational-pattern of the faithless-and-perverse-generation Sirach 16:6 names the substance for.'),

  -- Thread 5: the-just-man-as-son-of-yahuah-condemned-and-vindicated-in-wisdom-of-solomon-2
  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 22, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 13,
   '*He professeth to have the knowledge of Yahuah (God): and he calls himself the child of Yahuah (God).* Wisdom of Solomon 2:13 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the just-man-as-the-child-of-Yahuah substance — the credential the wicked''s-grievance-passage Wisdom of Solomon 2:12-20 carries throughout. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:22''s second-passion-prediction (*the Son of Adam shall be betrayed into the hands of men: and they shall kill him*), read against the just-spoken Father''s-voice declaring the King at v.5 (*this is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased*). The Son-of-Yahuah-credential the Father''s-voice declares is the substance Wisdom of Solomon 2 had named the wicked''s-grievance-against-the-righteous-one for at the prefiguring-register. The framework reads the verse in continuity with Tehillim (Psalm) 2:7''s *thou art my Son; this day have I begotten thee* the Father''s-voice combines into the declaration — the Davidic-Royal-Son the second-Psalm names is the Son-of-Yahuah Wisdom of Solomon 2 prefigures the persecution-against; the second-passion-prediction names the operative-fulfillment.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 22, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 16,
   '*We are esteemed of him as counterfeits: he abstaineth from our ways as from filthiness: he pronounceth the end of the just to be blessed, and makes his boast that Yahuah (God) is his father.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:16 names the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the wicked''s-grievance-against-the-righteous-one substance — the King''s-very-existence-as-the-indictment-of-the-counterfeit-credentialing the King''s-Matt-23-woes will articulate explicitly. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:22-23''s second-passion-prediction. The Pharisaic-and-Sadducean-second-Temple-aristocracy that will deliver-the-King-up-into-the-hands-of-men reads the King''s-very-existence as the indictment of their counterfeit-religious-credentialing; the wisdom-stream had named the architecture in the prefiguring-passage. The substance the King names at v.22 — that he will be delivered-up and killed — operates in the architecture Wisdom of Solomon 2 had prefigured at the wisdom-stream-level centuries before. (Threaded continuity with S146-Matt-16:21 — same prefiguring-passage, different application: at Matt 16:21 the application is to the religious-system''s persecution; at Matt 17:22-23 the application is to the categorical-Son-and-Father architecture the temple-tax-pericope at vv.24-27 will then unfold.)'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 26, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 18,
   '*For if the just man be the son of Yahuah (God), he will help him, and deliver him from the hand of his enemies.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:18 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the just-man-as-the-son-of-Yahuah substance the temple-tax-pericope''s categorical-architecture rests upon. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:26''s *then are the children free.* The King is the Son of the One whose Temple this is — the temple-tax is the Father''s-tax to the Father''s-house; the Son does not pay the Father''s-tax to the Father''s-house by the categorical-architecture-of-who-the-Son-is. Wisdom of Solomon 2:18 had named the just-man-as-the-son-of-Yahuah substance in the prefiguring-passage; the King''s-question to Kefa (Peter) (*of whom do the kings of the earth take custom or tribute? of their own children, or of strangers?*) draws the operative-conclusion the wisdom-stream had named the architecture for: the children-of-the-King are categorically-free of the King''s-tax. The framework reads this in continuity with John 20:17''s *my Father, and your Father; my Elohim (God), and your Elohim (God)* — the Father''s-Son-by-incarnation and the Father''s-sons-by-adoption-through-the-Son are both categorically-free of the temple-tax by the architecture-of-the-Father''s-household.'),

  ('canon', 'matthew', 17, 27, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 20,
   '*Let us condemn him with a shameful death: for by his own saying he shall be respected.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:20 names the wisdom-stream''s direct verbal-anchor for the shameful-death substance that the categorically-free-Son walks-toward at the temple-tax-pericope''s closing. The framework reads the verse against Matt 17:27''s *notwithstanding, lest we should offend them, go thou to the sea, and cast an hook, and take up the fish that first cometh up; and when thou hast opened his mouth, thou shalt find a piece of money: that take, and give unto them for me and thee.* The categorically-exempt-King chooses to pay the half-shekel-atonement-money at the small-domestic-scale; the same categorically-exempt-King walks toward the shameful-death-payment-of-the-atonement-substance at the cross-scale. Wisdom of Solomon 2:20 names the shameful-death the categorically-free-Son walks-into voluntarily; the half-shekel-from-the-fish''s-mouth is the architectural-rehearsal-in-miniature; the cross is the full-payment Hebrews 7:27 names as *he did once, when he offered up himself.* The framework reads the substance in continuity with the cause-and-effect-of-grace per the *Grace, the Way, the New Heart, and the Mercy of Depart* section of framework-deep.md — grace is the door-home, opened by the categorically-exempt-One''s-voluntary-walking-into-the-shameful-death-substance the categorically-bound owed. (Threaded continuity with S146-Matt-16:21 — same verbal-anchor, different scope: at Matt 16:21 the verbal-anchor lands the passion-prediction-itself; at Matt 17:27 the verbal-anchor lands the temple-tax-pericope''s pre-figuring of the same shameful-death-payment at the small-domestic-scale.)')

)
INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, 'extras'::content_tier
  FROM input i
  JOIN _s154_xref_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug   = i.src_edition
                           AND sv.book_slug      = i.src_slug
                           AND sv.chapter_number = i.src_ch
                           AND sv.verse_number   = i.src_v
  JOIN _s154_xref_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug   = i.tgt_edition
                           AND tv.book_slug      = i.tgt_slug
                           AND tv.chapter_number = i.tgt_ch
                           AND tv.verse_number   = i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insert 5 new extras-tier threads.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Thread 1 (sort 307): the-formless-father-and-the-formed-son-witnessed-in-ascension-of-isaiah
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'the-formless-father-and-the-formed-son-witnessed-in-ascension-of-isaiah',
       'The Formless-Father and the Formed-Son — Ascension of Isaiah 9-10''s seventh-heaven witness to the transfiguration (FRAMEWORK-MAJOR)',
       'Matt 17:1-8''s transfiguration — the King''s-face-shining-as-the-sun, raiment-white-as-the-light, the bright-cloud-overshadowing, the Father''s-voice declaring *this is my beloved Son*, and the final *Yahusha (Jesus) only* — read against the external-witness-articulation of the Formless-Father / Formed-Son nature-of-God-teaching Ascension of Isaiah 9-10 carries in the seventh-heaven-vision. Five moves: AI 9:27 names the Lord-standing-before-the-Great-Glory whose-glory-surpassed-that-of-all the angels-and-archangels of the six-lower-heavens (the Formed-Son in pre-incarnational standing-position); AI 9:33 names another Glorious-One who-was-like-Him (the Beloved beside the Lord — the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Father-Son architecture); AI 9:37 names the Great-Glory the eye-of-the-prophet-cannot-bear-to-look-upon (the Formless-Father per the framework''s nature-of-God reading); AI 10:7 names THE direct verbal-anchor — the Father-of-my-Lord speaking-to-my-Lord-Messiah-who-will-be-called-Yahusha (the same Father-speaking-to-the-Son architecture the transfiguration enacts at Matt 17:5 the Father''s-voice from the bright-cloud); AI 10:9-10 names the Beloved''s-kenotic-descent — becoming-like-the-likeness-of-each-heaven through which he descends (the kenosis-architecture Philippians 2:6-7 names at the apostolic-register and the transfiguration shows the brief-pulling-back-of-the-servant-form-veil for). The framework reads the cluster as FRAMEWORK-MAJOR. Per Yoshi''s S32 sourcing-decision (api/seed.py:EDITION_PROFILES["ascension-isaiah"]), AI is the *first witness* aligning with the framework''s Formless-Father / Formed-of-the-Formless teaching — pre-Nicene, late-1st / early-2nd CE, before the Constantine-era Trinity-construct hardened. The wisdom-stream and the gospel cohere at the architecture the transfiguration shows the disciples in compressed-foretaste-form.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'complete_study', 307
  FROM _s154_xref_lookup sv, _s154_xref_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug = 'canon' AND sv.book_slug = 'matthew' AND sv.chapter_number = 17 AND sv.verse_number = 1
   AND ev.edition_slug = 'canon' AND ev.book_slug = 'matthew' AND ev.chapter_number = 17 AND ev.verse_number = 8
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- Thread 2 (sort 308): the-son-of-adam-glorified-in-1-enoch-throne-vision-and-parables
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'the-son-of-adam-glorified-in-1-enoch-throne-vision-and-parables',
       'The Son of Adam in glorified-form — 1 Enoch''s throne-vision (ch 14) and Son-of-Adam Parables (ch 46, 49, 62) (FRAMEWORK-MAJOR)',
       'Matt 17:2-6''s transfiguration-substance — the King''s-face-shining + raiment-white + bright-cloud + Father''s-voice + disciples-falling-on-the-face — read against the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the glorified-Son-of-Adam in heavenly-throne-vision form. Five moves: 1 Enoch 14:20 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the *raiment whiter than snow* substance (*the Great Glory sat thereon, and His raiment shone more brightly than the sun and was whiter than any snow*) the transfiguration shows at the form-of-the-King-on-the-mountain; 1 Enoch 14:21 names the no-flesh-could-behold-Him substance the disciples'' fall-on-the-face at v.6 operates within; 1 Enoch 46:1 names the Head-of-Days-with-the-One-whose-countenance-had-the-appearance-of-a-man Father-and-Son architecture the Father''s-voice at v.5 articulates; 1 Enoch 49:2 names the Elect-One-standing-before-Yahuah-of-Spirits substance the Beloved-Son-on-the-mountain occupies; 1 Enoch 62:5 names the Son-of-Adam-sitting-on-the-throne-of-his-glory substance the transfiguration shows in pre-resurrection-foretaste-form. The framework reads the cluster as FRAMEWORK-MAJOR for the Son-of-Adam architecture per Red Line #12. The transfiguration is the disciples'' pre-resurrection-foretaste of what 1 Enoch had named at the heavenly-throne-register centuries before — the Tanakh-glorified-form-substance carried-through Daniel 7:9''s Ancient-of-Days-whose-garment-was-white-as-snow + Daniel 10:5-6''s Man-Clothed-in-Linen + Hitgalut (Revelation) 1:13-16''s *one like unto the Son of Adam* with the kaph-comparative preserved (the disciple Yochanan (John) is the disciple at BOTH the transfiguration AND the Patmos-vision; the substance is the same Formed-One). The wisdom-stream and the Tanakh and the gospel and the apostolic-vision all witness the same glorified-Son-of-Adam architecture.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'complete_study', 308
  FROM _s154_xref_lookup sv, _s154_xref_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug = 'canon' AND sv.book_slug = 'matthew' AND sv.chapter_number = 17 AND sv.verse_number = 2
   AND ev.edition_slug = 'canon' AND ev.book_slug = 'matthew' AND ev.chapter_number = 17 AND ev.verse_number = 6
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- Thread 3 (sort 309): eliyahu-as-reproof-prophet-turning-the-heart-in-sirach-48
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'eliyahu-as-reproof-prophet-turning-the-heart-in-sirach-48',
       'Eliyahu (Elijah) as reproof-prophet turning the heart — Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48''s wisdom-stream witness to the King''s Matt 17:10-13 identification of Yochanan (John) as the Eliyahu (Elijah)-pattern-prophet',
       'Matt 17:10-13''s coming-down-from-the-mountain dialogue — the disciples'' scribal-eschatology-question (*why then say the scribes that Eliyahu (Elijah) must first come?*) and the King''s both-fulfillments answer (future-tense *Eliyahu (Elijah) truly shall first come, and restore all things* + past-tense *Eliyahu (Elijah) is come already* identified at v.13 with Yochanan (John) the Immerser) — read against the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Eliyahu (Elijah)-as-prophet-of-reproofs-turning-the-heart substance in Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48. Three moves: Sirach 48:1 names THE direct verbal-anchor for the Eliyahu (Elijah)-prophet-as-fire substance (*then stood up Elias the prophet as fire, and his word burned like a lamp*); Sirach 48:4 names the Eliyahu (Elijah)-honoured-in-wondrous-deeds substance (*O Elias, how were you honoured in your wondrous deeds! and who may glory like to you!*); Sirach 48:10 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the turn-the-heart-of-the-father-unto-the-son substance from Malachi 4:5-6 — and adds the *set up the tribes of Yashar''el (Jacob)* substance the apostolic Acts 3:21 *times of restitution of all things* will articulate (*who were ordained for reproofs in their times ... and to turn the heart of the father unto the son, and to set up the tribes of Yashar''el (Jacob)*). The framework reads the cluster in continuity with Red Line #11''s ingathering-of-the-paternal-blood-remnant-of-all-twelve-tribes architecture — Sirach 48:10''s explicit naming of the *set up the tribes of Yashar''el (Jacob)* substance is the wisdom-stream''s direct corroboration that the Eliyahu (Elijah)-restoration the prophets named IS the gathering-of-the-scattered-seed the framework reads across the prophetic-corpus. Yochanan (John) the Immerser at the first-coming carried the Eliyahu (Elijah)-pattern of reproof-against-the-religious-system (the Pharisees-and-Sadducees of Matt 3:7''s *generation of vipers*) and against the apostate-king (Herod-Antipas and Herodias, the Achav (Ahab) and Izevel (Jezebel) of the first-century-recapitulation); the future-tense Eliyahu (Elijah) of Hitgalut (Revelation) 11''s two-witnesses will carry the same pattern at the second-coming with the broader-restoration-of-all-things the prophets had named.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'complete_study', 309
  FROM _s154_xref_lookup sv, _s154_xref_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug = 'canon' AND sv.book_slug = 'matthew' AND sv.chapter_number = 17 AND sv.verse_number = 10
   AND ev.edition_slug = 'canon' AND ev.book_slug = 'matthew' AND ev.chapter_number = 17 AND ev.verse_number = 13
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- Thread 4 (sort 310): the-faithless-and-perverse-generation-in-sirach-wisdom-of-solomon-and-2-esdras
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'the-faithless-and-perverse-generation-in-sirach-wisdom-of-solomon-and-2-esdras',
       'The faithless and perverse generation — wisdom-stream witness to Matt 17:17 from Sirach 16, Wisdom of Solomon 5, and 2 Esdras 7',
       'Matt 17:17''s *O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you?* — the King''s-rebuke at the foot of the mountain after the disciples-could-not-cast-out-the-demon — read against the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the long-arc-of-the-faithless-generation substance the King''s Greek (*genea apistos kai diestrammenē*) carries-forward from Mosheh''s (Moses'') song against the wilderness-generation (Devarim (Deuteronomy) 32:5, 20). Four moves: Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 16:1 names the wisdom-stream''s opening of the unprofitable-and-ungodly-generation diagnostic (*desire not a multitude of unprofitable children, neither delight in ungodly sons*) the Sirach 16:1-14 unit unfolds; Sirach 16:6 names the consequences-on-the-rebellious-nation substance (*in the congregation of the ungodly shall a fire be kindled; and in a rebellious nation wrath is set on fire*) tying the wilderness-judgment-pattern forward; Wisdom of Solomon 5:6 names the post-judgment-confession-of-the-ungodly substance (*therefore have we erred from the way of truth*) the day-of-vindication-of-the-righteous-will-reveal; 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:48 names the corporate-inheritance-of-the-Adam-fall substance running across the generations (*O thou Adam, what hast thou done? for though it was thou that sinned, the fall was not thine alone, but ours also that come of thee*). The framework reads the cluster as the wisdom-stream''s direct corroboration of the long-arc the King names at v.17 — the faithlessness reaches the King''s-day in the religious-system of the leadership and the broader-people''s-disposition; the kingdom-cure is the new-heart of Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27, the Spirit-internalized-Torah breaking-the-generational-pattern, NOT the inherited-Christian-Augustinian original-sin doctrine that collapses the architecture into a forensic-substitutionary-juridical-transaction. The mustard-seed-faith of the right-substance the King teaches at vv.20-21 is the qualitative-substance that operates against the generation-pattern Sirach 16 + Wisdom of Solomon 5 + 2 Esdras 7 names the architecture for.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'complete_study', 310
  FROM _s154_xref_lookup sv, _s154_xref_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug = 'canon' AND sv.book_slug = 'matthew' AND sv.chapter_number = 17 AND sv.verse_number = 17
   AND ev.edition_slug = 'canon' AND ev.book_slug = 'matthew' AND ev.chapter_number = 17 AND ev.verse_number = 20
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- Thread 5 (sort 311): the-just-man-as-son-of-yahuah-condemned-and-vindicated-in-wisdom-of-solomon-2
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'the-just-man-as-son-of-yahuah-condemned-and-vindicated-in-wisdom-of-solomon-2',
       'The just man as son of Yahuah condemned and vindicated — Wisdom of Solomon 2''s prefiguring-passage tying Matt 17:22-23''s second-passion-prediction to vv.24-27''s temple-tax pre-figuring',
       'Matt 17:22-27''s twinned passage — the second-passion-prediction at vv.22-23 (*the Son of Adam shall be betrayed into the hands of men: and they shall kill him, and the third day he shall be raised again*) AND the temple-tax-pericope at vv.24-27 (*then are the children free* + the categorically-exempt-King paying the half-shekel-atonement-money-from-the-fish''s-mouth) — read together against the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the just-man-as-the-son-of-Yahuah persecuted-and-condemned-with-a-shameful-death and vindicated-in-the-resurrection substance in Wisdom of Solomon 2:13-20. Four moves: Wisdom of Solomon 2:13 names the wisdom-stream''s direct verbal-anchor for the just-man-as-the-child-of-Yahuah substance (*he professeth to have the knowledge of Yahuah (God): and he calls himself the child of Yahuah (God)*); Wisdom of Solomon 2:16 names the wicked''s-grievance-against-the-righteous-one (*he maketh his boast that Yahuah (God) is his father*) — the King''s-very-existence-as-the-indictment-of-the-counterfeit-credentialing the religious-system carries; Wisdom of Solomon 2:18 names THE direct verbal-anchor for the categorically-free-son-of-Yahuah substance the temple-tax-pericope''s architecture rests upon (*if the just man be the son of Yahuah (God), he will help him*); Wisdom of Solomon 2:20 names THE direct verbal-anchor for the shameful-death the categorically-free-Son walks-toward (*let us condemn him with a shameful death: for by his own saying he shall be respected*). The framework reads the cluster as the wisdom-stream''s direct prefiguring of the architecture the King''s-twinned-passage articulates: the same just-man-as-the-son-of-Yahuah Wisdom of Solomon 2 names is the One whom Matt 17:22-23 names as the about-to-be-delivered-up-and-killed Son-of-Adam AND the One whom Matt 17:24-27 names as the categorically-exempt-Son-paying-the-atonement-money-from-the-fish''s-mouth. The half-shekel-from-the-fish''s-mouth is the architectural-rehearsal-in-miniature of what the cross-payment-of-the-shameful-death will complete at full-scale (Hebrews 7:27''s *this he did once, when he offered up himself*). The categorically-exempt-One pays-the-atonement-substance the categorically-bound owed, both at the small-domestic-scale and at the cross-scale; the wisdom-stream had named the architecture in the prefiguring-passage. The framework reads the substance in continuity with the cause-and-effect-of-grace per the *Grace, the Way, the New Heart, and the Mercy of Depart* section of framework-deep.md — grace is the door-home, opened by the categorically-exempt-One''s voluntary walking-into-the-shameful-death the categorically-bound owed. (Threaded continuity with S146-Matt-16:21 — the same Wisdom of Solomon 2 prefiguring-passage applied to the first-passion-prediction; Matt 17 carries-forward to the second-prediction AND extends the prefiguring-application to the temple-tax pericope''s categorical-architecture.)',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'complete_study', 311
  FROM _s154_xref_lookup sv, _s154_xref_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug = 'canon' AND sv.book_slug = 'matthew' AND sv.chapter_number = 17 AND sv.verse_number = 22
   AND ev.edition_slug = 'canon' AND ev.book_slug = 'matthew' AND ev.chapter_number = 17 AND ev.verse_number = 27
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

